{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve for \\( c_5 \\), we start by defining the sequences \\( a_n \\) and \\( b_n \\) more explicitly. Let the arithmetic sequence \\( a_n \\) be given by \\( a_n = a + (n-1)d \\) and the geometric sequence \\( b_n \\) be given by \\( b_n = br^{n-1} \\). Therefore, the sequence \\( c_n \\) is defined as \\( c_n = a_n + b_n = a + (n-1)d + br^{n-1} \\).\n\nWe are given the following values:\n\\[ c_1 = 1, \\]\n\\[ c_2 = 4, \\]\n\\[ c_3 = 15, \\]\n\\[ c_4 = 2. \\]\n\nFirst, we substitute \\( n = 1 \\) into the expression for \\( c_n \\):\n\\[ c_1 = a + b = 1. \\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\( n = 2 \\):\n\\[ c_2 = a + d + br = 4. \\]\n\nThen, we substitute \\( n = 3 \\):\n\\[ c_3 = a + 2d + br^2 = 15. \\]\n\nFinally, we substitute \\( n = 4 \\):\n\\[ c_4 = a + 3d + br^3 = 2. \\]\n\nWe now have the following system of equations:\n1. \\( a + b = 1, \\)\n2. \\( a + d + br = 4, \\)\n3. \\( a + 2d + br^2 = 15, \\)\n4. \\( a + 3d + br^3 = 2. \\)\n\nFrom the first equation, we can express \\( a \\) in terms of \\( b \\):\n\\[ a = 1 - b. \\]\n\nSubstitute \\( a = 1 - b \\) into the second equation:\n\\[ 1 - b + d + br = 4, \\]\n\\[ d + br - b = 3, \\]\n\\[ d + b(r-1) = 3. \\quad \\text{(Equation 5)} \\]\n\nSubstitute \\( a = 1 - b \\) into the third equation:\n\\[ 1 - b + 2d + br^2 = 15, \\]\n\\[ 2d + br^2 - b = 14, \\]\n\\[ 2d + b(r^2 - 1) = 14. \\quad \\text{(Equation 6)} \\]\n\nSubstitute \\( a = 1 - b \\) into the fourth equation:\n\\[ 1 - b + 3d + br^3 = 2, \\]\n\\[ 3d + br^3 - b = 1, \\]\n\\[ 3d + b(r^3 - 1) = 1. \\quad \\text{(Equation 7)} \\]\n\nWe now have three equations in terms of \\( d \\) and \\( b \\):\n\\[ d + b(r-1) = 3, \\]\n\\[ 2d + b(r^2 - 1) = 14, \\]\n\\[ 3d + b(r^3 - 1) = 1. \\]\n\nWe can solve these equations by elimination. First, multiply Equation 5 by 2:\n\\[ 2d + 2b(r-1) = 6. \\]\nSubtract this from Equation 6:\n\\[ (2d + b(r^2 - 1)) - (2d + 2b(r-1)) = 14 - 6, \\]\n\\[ b(r^2 - 1) - 2b(r-1) = 8, \\]\n\\[ b(r^2 - 1 - 2r + 2) = 8, \\]\n\\[ b(r^2 - 2r + 1) = 8, \\]\n\\[ b(r-1)^2 = 8. \\quad \\text{(Equation 8)} \\]\n\n","prefix_end":1896,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,369,17767,272,62,20,1124,701,582,1191,553,26312,279,23700,17767,264,1089,1124,8,323,17767,293,1089,1124,8,803,20975,13,6771,279,34784,8500,17767,264,1089,1124,8,387,2661,553,17767,264,1089,284,264,488,320,77,12,16,65259,1124,8,323,279,52484,8500,17767,293,1089,1124,8,387,2661,553,17767,293,1089,284,1411,47822,77,12,16,92,1124,568,15277,11,279,8500,17767,272,1089,1124,8,374,4512,438,17767,272,1089,284,264,1089,488,293,1089,284,264,488,320,77,12,16,65259,488,1411,47822,77,12,16,92,1124,3593,1654,525,2661,279,2701,2750,510,78045,272,62,16,284,220,16,11,1124,921,78045,272,62,17,284,220,19,11,1124,921,78045,272,62,18,284,220,16,20,11,1124,921,78045,272,62,19,284,220,17,13,1124,2533,5338,11,582,27679,17767,308,284,220,16,1124,8,1119,279,7493,369,17767,272,1089,1124,982,78045,272,62,16,284,264,488,293,284,220,16,13,1124,2533,5847,11,582,27679,17767,308,284,220,17,1124,982,78045,272,62,17,284,264,488,294,488,1411,284,220,19,13,1124,2533,12209,11,582,27679,17767,308,284,220,18,1124,982,78045,272,62,18,284,264,488,220,17,67,488,1411,61,17,284,220,16,20,13,1124,2533,23949,11,582,27679,17767,308,284,220,19,1124,982,78045,272,62,19,284,264,488,220,18,67,488,1411,61,18,284,220,17,13,1124,2533,1654,1431,614,279,2701,1849,315,37906,510,16,13,17767,264,488,293,284,220,16,11,1124,340,17,13,17767,264,488,294,488,1411,284,220,19,11,1124,340,18,13,17767,264,488,220,17,67,488,1411,61,17,284,220,16,20,11,1124,340,19,13,17767,264,488,220,18,67,488,1411,61,18,284,220,17,13,1124,692,3830,279,1156,23606,11,582,646,3158,17767,264,1124,8,304,3793,315,17767,293,1124,982,78045,264,284,220,16,481,293,13,1124,2533,3136,7660,17767,264,284,220,16,481,293,1124,8,1119,279,2086,23606,510,78045,220,16,481,293,488,294,488